  ('verification-17', 'Quy trình kiểm chứng', 'Giới hạn và cảnh báo', '## Giới hạn và cảnh báo

- Không có Supabase CLI hoặc `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` trong môi trường này. Production project identity, migration ledger, backup/PITR, schema/RLS, Auth hosted, Edge status và production smoke tests chưa xác minh.
  → **Cập nhật 2026-10-03:** Supabase CLI đã hoạt động. Production ledger (001–037 applied), Auth config (`config diff` match), Edge Functions (manage-users v10, ai-assist v3, process-message v1), backup (FREE plan, no PITR), và Vercel smoke script đều đã xác minh read-only. Migration `038_knowledge_reseed` là local/pending duy nhất.
- Build/test không kết nối Supabase production, không thay đổi tài khoản thật, Auth credentials, Edge deployments hay dữ liệu thật.
- Không có khóa/provider AI cấu hình. Camera, OCR, microphone, upload Storage HTTP, máy in thật, và cài PWA trên điện thoại cần kiểm tra thủ công.
- Migration 018 chứa mật khẩu OWNER mặc định dạng cứng và ghi giá trị đó vào notice. File được giữ lại trong worktree nhưng loại khỏi checkpoint Git; không được áp dụng.

Xem `docs/PRODUCTION_RELEASE.md` để biết bảng migration, trạng thái production và bước tiếp theo an toàn. Xem `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md` để biết phạm vi tính năng và giới hạn kiểm thử.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/VERIFICATION.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-preamble', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', null, '# Customer communication architecture

Phase 1 adds a provider-agnostic post-sale thank-you workflow. AI, marketing automation, bulk outreach, payment and debt automations are out of scope.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-1', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', 'Sale event and outbox', '## Sale event and outbox

`public.sell_vehicle` remains the authoritative atomic sale operation. After it inserts the completed sale and marks the vehicle SOLD, it writes one `SALE_THANK_YOU` row to `public.message_outbox` in the same database transaction. The unique `(event_type, sale_id, channel)` constraint prevents duplicate events for a sale/channel. No external request runs in PostgreSQL. The caller commits the sale before the UI invokes `process-message` in the background.

The message is queued only when customer messaging, sale thank-you automation, and a primary channel are enabled and the phone normalizes to a valid Vietnamese mobile number. Otherwise an auditable `SKIPPED` row and CRM history item explain the safe skip. Defaults are disabled.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-2', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', 'Provider worker and status', '## Provider worker and status

`supabase/functions/process-message` authenticates the caller and claims one eligible queued job through a server-authorized RPC. A canonical `MessagingProvider` interface accepts the recipient, channel, template variables, and idempotency key. It supports only explicit `MESSAGE_PROVIDER_MODE=MOCK`, which records a `mock_...` identifier and `SENT` state as simulated success. The disabled provider fails closed and records a permanent provider-not-configured failure. This function has no production provider implementation and must not be treated as real delivery. `SENT` means accepted by the mock; callbacks can later advance a provider message to `DELIVERED`.

Statuses are `QUEUED`, `PROCESSING`, `SENT`, `DELIVERED`, `FAILED`, `SKIPPED`, and `CANCELLED`. Transient failures use up to three attempts with bounded exponential delay. Invalid phone and missing provider configuration are permanent. OWNER/MANAGER may manually retry eligible failed jobs; retry reuses the same outbox/history row and starts a new bounded attempt window. Provider-not-configured and invalid-phone skips are not retryable.

The sale flow invokes the worker once after commit. No hosted scheduler or durable queue trigger is installed in this phase, so transient retries remain safely queued until a later trusted worker invocation. A production provider rollout must include a verified scheduled/drain trigger.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-3', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', 'Communication history', '## Communication history

`public.customer_communications` is durable CRM history, joined to the existing completed sales by normalized Vietnamese phone. It stores only a short message preview, provider identifier, status and lifecycle timestamps. It does not store provider payloads, credentials, or sale financial data. Customer history and sale detail read through role-checked RPCs.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-4', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', 'Settings and security', '## Settings and security

Messaging controls live on `system_settings` and can only be changed by OWNER through the existing settings RPC boundary. Client settings include enablement, thank-you automation, preferred/fallback channel, store brand and support phone. No credential fields exist in client settings. Outbox/history tables have RLS enabled and direct grants revoked; RPCs enforce active-role checks. Provider credentials, when a real integration is approved, belong only in Supabase Edge Function secrets.

Audit events include `AUTO_MESSAGE_QUEUED`, `MESSAGE_SENT`, `MESSAGE_FAILED`, `MESSAGE_RETRIED`, `MESSAGE_MANUALLY_RETRIED`, and `MESSAGE_SETTING_CHANGED`; they contain operational status only.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-5', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', 'Activating a real provider', '## Activating a real provider

Production sending is not configured. Activation requires an approved Zalo ZNS or SMS account, reviewed template and consent/eligibility policy, provider-specific Edge Function implementation, server-side secrets, retry/error mapping, delivery callback verification, and hosted tests. Do not add keys to Vite variables, SQL rows, logs, or source control. Until those steps are complete, keep sending disabled; mock results are workflow verification only.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('communication-architecture-6', 'Kiến trúc liên lạc khách hàng', 'Future AI integration', '## Future AI integration

Future AI may draft, personalize, or summarize communication, but it must not control sale transactions or become a delivery dependency. Automation decides when to contact; AI may suggest content; this outbox and provider boundary own delivery and history.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-preamble', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', null, '# Xe CRM AI extraction and read assistant — prepared interface

Status on 2026-10-01: implemented locally and verified with mocked provider/Edge tests, plus the `knowledge_base` corpus and its PGLite checks. No provider key has been configured, no external images/text have been sent, and no Edge deployment or hosted business mutation has been performed by this work.

Contract revision 2026-10-08: the `odometer` task was deleted and every brand / model-line / variant / engine-number / odometer / asking-price field was removed from the extraction schemas, matching the permanent column purge on `public.vehicles` (`docs/VEHICLE_FIELD_PURGE_IMPACT.md`). Clients that still send `task: ''odometer''` are refused by `validateInput`, which guards the task allowlist and the consent flag with the same `400 EXPLICIT_PROCESSING_CONSENT_REQUIRED` — the failure is loud, never a silently ignored field.

Contract revision 2026-10-13: the smart camera''s vehicle-photo mode (`scan_mode: ''vehicle''`, which suggested `vehicle_type` / `color` / `year` from a motorcycle''s appearance) was deleted outright at the shop owner''s request. `vehicle_scan` now accepts only `scan_mode` `identifiers` (default, plate + frame) and `identity` (CCCD, OWNER/MANAGER only), and its output schema is exactly `license_plate`, `frame_number`, `identity_number`, `uncertain_characters`. Clients that still send `scan_mode: ''vehicle''` are refused with `400 INVALID_SCAN_MODE` — loud, never a silent downgrade. `vehicle_document` remains the only task that reads color and year, and only from vehicle paperwork.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-1', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', 'Request and response', '## Request and response

Invoke the `ai-assist` Supabase Edge Function with the existing authenticated user session. The frontend must display a clear processing action and send `consent: true` only after the user invokes it. The function rejects unauthenticated, disabled, outside-schedule, deleted and temporary-password users before provider processing.

```ts
type Request = {
  task: ''receipt'' | ''vehicle_document'' | ''vehicle_scan'' | ''license_plate'' | ''voice'' | ''business_question'' | ''copilot'';
  consent: true;
  vehicle_id?: string; // existing UUID context takes priority over model-selected context
  mode?: ''deterministic'' | ''llm''; // copilot only; ''llm'' requires the OWNER role
  image?: { mime_type: ''image/jpeg'' | ''image/png'' | ''image/webp''; base64: string };
  text?: string; // a voice transcript, business question or copilot question, maximum 2,000 characters
};
```

Image tasks accept one cropped/compressed image, maximum 2 MiB decoded. Text tasks require text and reject images. The server bounds streamed request bodies to 3 MB, checks image signatures, validates the exact request fields, and never persists the image or logs raw documents, transcripts or provider output.

Extraction returns:

```json
{
  "kind": "draft",
  "task": "receipt",
  "vehicle_id": "existing-vehicle-uuid-or-null",
  "draft": { "amount": 850000, "date": null, "merchant": null, "description": null, "expense_type": null },
  "human_confirmation_required": true,
  "warnings": ["Kiểm tra lại từng trường trước khi lưu. Số khung và các số tiền cần được xác nhận."]
}
```

Every field is nullable when uncertain. `vehicle_document` returns frame number, plate, color and year. `vehicle_scan` (the smart camera at `/capture`) returns plate and frame only: copied exactly as printed with the plate normalised to `59A1-234.56` — anything unclear must be null, so the client never receives an invented value; `identity_number` is added solely for the CCCD `identity` scan mode. **There is no brand, model line, variant, engine number, odometer or asking-price field anywhere in this contract.** Those vehicle columns were dropped permanently on 2026-10-08 (see `docs/VEHICLE_FIELD_PURGE_IMPACT.md`), the `odometer` task was deleted outright, and the provider prompt states the same rule so a stale model cannot resurrect the fields. The vehicle type is not an extraction target either: staff pick it from the shop catalogue (`public.vehicle_types`). The plate task returns only the plate. Voice returns a limited intent (`CREATE_ACQUISITION`, `ADD_VEHICLE_EXPENSE`, `PREPARE_SALE`, `UNKNOWN`) and explicit draft fields (`frame_number`, `license_plate`, `color`, `purchase_price`, `amount`, `description`, `expense_type`, `date`). It never executes a command and **never carries a selling price** — `sale_price` exists only on the sale form, typed by staff. Browser speech recognition can supply the `text` field; typed text remains the fallback. Server transcription is not implemented.

The frontend must apply a draft only to an editable form, retain existing vehicle context, show extracted values for review, and call the normal secure business RPC only after human confirmation. A draft is not a completed acquisition, expense, payment or sale. No write/action-agent endpoint exists.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-2', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', 'Read assistant and permissions', '## Read assistant and permissions

Business questions are converted into a validated read plan. The server executes a fixed read allowlist with the current user''s JWT, then returns actual RPC data as `facts`. Model-generated numbers or prose answers are not used. Database results are not sent to the external provider.

Supported plans: inventory counts, monthly acquisition counts, monthly sale counts, monthly revenue, monthly gross profit, inventory aging, vehicle search, vehicle expenses and vehicle history. These currently map to `dashboard`, `list_vehicles` and `get_vehicle`; pagination limits search to 25 results. Unsupported questions return `available:false`. Failed retrieval returns `503 DATA_UNAVAILABLE`.

`OWNER` can request all supported plans. Revenue and expense queries require `OWNER`/`MANAGER`. Profit requires `OWNER` or a `MANAGER` with `can_view_financials`. Staff can search/view operational summaries, but cannot use the assistant to bypass restricted costs/profit. Expense extraction/drafts require management rights. Vehicle-document, smart-camera `vehicle_scan` and lifecycle voice drafts require operating rights. Every database RPC still enforces the server''s existing authorization.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-3', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', 'Copilot mode (`task: ''copilot''`)', '## Copilot mode (`task: ''copilot''`)

The copilot answers free-form questions about the shop and always returns evidence. The function itself is read-only: no draft, no write, and no provider call unless the OWNER explicitly asks for prose mode.

Retrieval (`src/features/copilot/CopilotPage.tsx` → `supabase/functions/ai-assist/copilot.ts`) runs first and always:

1. `search_knowledge` ranks documentation sections the caller''s audience tier may read.
2. Keyword intents (overview, inventory, acquisitions, recent sales, sales, daily cash, revenue, profit, aging, receivables, expenses, audit, customers, team, settings) call only the existing read RPCs — `dashboard`, `list_receivables`, `list_expenses`, `list_audit`, `list_profiles`, `get_settings`, `list_sales`, `list_customers`, `daily_reconciliation` — with the caller''s JWT, so RLS and `private.require_role` decide what is answerable. `daily_reconciliation` is the server''s own OWNER/MANAGER gate, so the cash intent is marked management-only.
3. When no intent yields a figure, a grounded fallback runs `global_search` on a detected plate, phone number, or quoted name, citing the matching vehicles, sales and customers directly.
4. Each returned figure is paired with a citation (`id`, `type`, `label`, `detail`, `route`) pointing at the exact screen that shows it (`/vehicles/:id`, `/sales/:id`, `/receivables`, `/expenses`, `/audit`, `/users`, `/customers`, `/settings`, `/docs/:slug`).

Questions naming a period resolve it in Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh before the read: `tháng 9`, `tháng này`, `tháng trước`, `2026-08`, `hôm nay`, `hôm qua`, `tuần này`, `quý 3`, `năm 2025` and `tháng 9 năm 2025` all set the `dashboard`/`list_sales` bounds.

Responses use `kind: ''copilot''`:

```json
{
  "kind": "copilot",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "available": true,
  "coverage": "both",
  "period": "Tháng 09/2026",
  "facts": [{ "label": "Xe đang tồn kho", "value": 7, "display": "7 xe", "citation": "m2" }],
  "citations": [{ "id": "m2", "type": "metric", "label": "Xe đang tồn kho", "detail": "Tháng 09/2026", "route": "/vehicles" }],
  "doc_excerpts": [{ "id": "d1", "title": "Checklist phát hành Cà Rem", "section": "Kiểm thử", "excerpt": "Chạy npm run check:db…" }],
  "answer_markdown": "- Xe đang tồn kho: **7 xe** [m2]",
  "suggestions": [{ "label": "Mở Sổ công nợ", "route": "/receivables" }],
  "insufficient": false,
  "warnings": []
}
```

`mode: ''llm''` is OWNER-only (`validateInput` rejects it for other roles with `LLM_MODE_OWNER_ONLY`). It adds a provider summary written **only over the evidence this request already retrieved** and uses `copilotSchema`/`validateGroundedAnswer`: the provider returns `answer_markdown`, `citation_ids` and `insufficient`; unknown citation ids, missing grounding, over-length prose or non-internal links are rejected and the handler falls back to the deterministic answer with a warning. The provider never receives credentials, raw rows outside the retrieved facts, or a write capability. `AI_ENABLED`, `AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY` and `AI_MODEL` are therefore optional for the copilot: deterministic answers work without any provider configuration, while a missing configuration simply downgrades `mode: ''llm''` to the grounded lookup.

The copilot limit is 30 requests per user per 10 minutes (other tasks remain at 10). Documentation is read through `search_knowledge`, `list_knowledge` and `get_knowledge_article`; see [supabase/API.md](../supabase/API.md) for the corpus and its audience tiers.

### Draft-to-save handoff (client-side, review-only)

`src/lib/shorthand/draftActions.ts` deterministically parses a command sentence typed into the copilot (also used by the `/assist` voice task when no provider is configured) into an editable draft proposal: "chi 500k thay nhot xe 59-B1 123.45" → vehicle expense, "ban cho anh Binh 30tr xe 59-B1 123.45" → sale draft, purchase shorthand → the existing `/intake` parser. Detection runs entirely in the browser, refuses questions and interrogations, requires a real plate for anything vehicle-bound, and never reaches this Edge Function. `DraftActionCard` only prefills the normal secure forms — `QuickExpenseModal`, the sale sheet (`SellVehiclePage` consumes `state.aiDraft` for customer name and phone only; `sale_price` and `initial_payment` always start empty because the system holds no price to copy) or the seeded notes box on `/intake` (`state.seedText` auto-parses) — and the write still happens through the existing confirmed RPC after the human reviews every field. Expense proposals render only for OWNER/MANAGER (`canManage`), sale and intake proposals only for operable roles. This is a UX handoff, not an action agent: no RPC executes without the forms'' own confirmation.

### Smart Camera recognition (`/capture` → `/intake`)

The smart camera is a local-first scanner (`src/lib/smartcam/`): recognition runs on-device and `vehicle_scan` (this Edge Function) is an optional, budgeted cloud fallback — never the default per-frame path. Every business decision stays client-side under the existing read RPCs:

0. Three layers per live scan tick, cheapest first: (a) ZXing QR/barcode decoding of the frame — free, multi-code (whole frame + lower band); a vehicle QR is verified against `get_vehicle` before it counts as a match; (b) Tesseract WASM OCR in a background worker — free, plate-band + sparse-text passes with contrast preprocessing, glyph-confusion candidate parsing gated by `@/lib/plate` validation, adaptive frame sampling (650 ms base, backoff to 2.4 s while starved, never overlapping passes) and stable-frame voting (a read fires only after ≥2 identical frames at ≥55 mean confidence, with scene-change reset); (c) the paid `vehicle_scan` cloud call only in a configured mode — default **`manual`** (explicit "AI đọc ảnh" button or user-initiated shot; `auto` fallback after six consecutive sharp unreadable ticks must be deliberately enabled), or `off`. Camera frames are never streamed; at most one image leaves the device per budgeted decision. The local layers extract identity strings only (plate/frame/QR): the camera reads **identifiers only** — vehicle-photo appearance recognition was deleted outright on 2026-10-13, and no on-device or cloud appearance model is claimed. There is no odometer capture flow at all: the bike''s mileage is nowhere in the record, so a photographed instrument cluster has no destination.
1. `recognition.ts` normalizes identifiers through `@/lib/plate` (canonical plate, stripped frame code; `source: "local" | "cloud"` records which layer produced the read), then `lookup.ts` resolves identity via `list_vehicles` re-filtered to exact canonical equality: one match → VERIFIED vehicle profile; no match → optional "Thu xe mới"; multiple or contradictory identifiers → ambiguous/conflict requiring manual verification. The success tone sounds only for a unique verified match (and only once per scan target); ambiguous or conflicting identity gets the review tone; "no match" is silent.
2. Each field carries a provenance status (VERIFIED / SUGGESTED / UNREADABLE / CONFLICT) that travels with the result and renders as badges in the camera and inline in the intake form.
3. "Thu xe mới" maps the single normalized result onto one existing `IntakeEntry` (`recognitionToIntakeEntry`) and navigates to `/intake` via `state.recognition` — no second intake parser, no parallel save API. The write remains the confirmed `validate_import_vehicles` → `import_vehicles` protocol; prices and customer data are never prefilled from the camera.
4. User-approved photos stay in memory/router state (sessionStorage drafts exclude images) and upload after the confirmed write through the existing storage gateway, keyed by the server-issued `vehicle_ids` that `import_vehicles` returns in the same transaction (stored in the operation receipt, so a reconciled replay carries them) — never a substring re-search of the inventory; the exact-match re-lookup is a last resort for legacy results and only when exactly one row matches. Upload failures are reported without touching the saved record. Auto-capture, on-device OCR, sound and auto-open are user settings.

### Cloud cost limits (`vehicle_scan` from the camera)

The only client code path that can invoke the paid provider for the camera is `api.assist({ task: ''vehicle_scan'' })` inside `SmartVehicleScan.cloudRead` — every frame analysis, lookup and photo operation is local or free-RPC. Each call is checked against a rolling one-hour browser ledger (`src/lib/smartcam/local/budget.ts`, key `xe_crm_smartcam_cloud_ledger_v1`): at most 6 cloud reads per hour overall and 1 per scan target per hour; manual/library shots get minute-granularity target keys. The ledger records latency and image bytes per call, the UI shows today''s usage against the limit, and blocked fallbacks surface an honest Vietnamese notice instead of silently spending. Consent to send images remains mandatory for any cloud call. **This browser ledger is friction, not a ceiling** — it resets with the device and cannot bound the organization. Server side, every request is already authenticated (`check_user_access` + profile role + task gate + per-user `throttle` of 10 requests/10 minutes before any provider call, plus the 2 MB image bound and `AI_ENABLED` as a global kill switch), but that throttle lives in isolate memory: it is per-isolate, not a shared or persistent org-wide budget. A true enforceable ceiling needs a server-side usage table (migration) and provider spending caps — until those are verified, cloud mode defaults to `manual`. Latency and JS heap usage (Chromium only) render in the on-screen metrics row; real device OCR accuracy, false-match rate and provider cost per 1,000 scans are live checks this repository cannot measure.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-4', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', 'Provider and operational configuration', '## Provider and operational configuration

The initial adapter uses OpenAI Responses with strict JSON schema, `store:false`, a 30-second timeout and an output token cap. The configured model must support image inputs and structured outputs. No model is chosen implicitly. Change the isolated `providerDraft` adapter to use a different provider without changing business RPCs or draft contracts.

Server-only environment settings:

- `AI_ENABLED=true`: explicit enablement; otherwise normal forms remain the available path.
- `AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY`: external provider credential; never use a `VITE_` variable.
- `AI_MODEL`: explicit compatible model identifier selected for this deployment.
- Existing `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` / publishable key: the function uses user JWTs and never reads a service-role credential.

Missing configuration returns `503 AI_NOT_CONFIGURED`. The UI should explain availability and retain manual entry. Do not automatically call the function on screen renders, normal search, validation or saving a simple form.

Usage logs contain only user UUID, task, model, token counts and duration. An initial per-isolate limit allows 10 requests per user per 10 minutes; this is not a distributed billing limit. Before production enablement, configure provider/project spending controls and, if needed, a shared rate limiter. Provider errors/refusals/incomplete or invalid outputs never become drafts or business writes.

`store:false` disables Responses application state storage; it does not independently establish Zero Data Retention or override provider abuse-monitoring obligations. Confirm the deployment''s provider/data-retention policy before enabling sensitive document processing. Supabase infrastructure can also have its own access/error logs, separate from application code.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-5', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', 'Sensitive capture separation', '## Sensitive capture separation

Vehicle-photo storage remains a private bucket with registered-image authorization and signed URLs. Registered ordinary vehicle photos are readable by active application users. Do not place identity documents or receipts into that bucket. Capture those in browser memory for explicit transient extraction; a future durable document workflow needs a separate restricted bucket and authorization policy.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ai-assist-contract-6', 'Hợp đồng AI trợ lý', 'Verification boundary', '## Verification boundary

Local tests cover actual Edge handler authentication, missing configuration, draft confirmation, restricted profit queries, grounded reads, request/image/output validation and absence of business writes. SQL tests separately verify temporary-password gating, real password-change proof, restricted acquisition costs and owner-only performance summaries. The copilot adds `tests/security/copilot.test.ts` (input contract, owner-only prose mode, evidence grounding, provider fallback), `tests/unit/copilot-ui.test.tsx` (Markdown/citation rendering stays escaped and internal), `tests/unit/copilot-draft-actions.test.tsx` (deterministic command parsing, question rejection, plate/phone guards, role-gated prefilled card), `tests/db/knowledge.test.mjs` (documentation tiers and read RPCs) and `tests/e2e/copilot.spec.mjs` (sidebar entry, clickable evidence, doc viewer). The smart camera adds `tests/security/ai-assist.test.ts` vehicle_scan cases (consent, role gate, exact-key/range output rejection), `tests/unit/smartcam.test.ts` (acceptance A/B/E/F/G at the pure-logic layer: identity resolution, conflict blocking, provenance, intake-entry mapping without invented fields, beep dedupe, draft roundtrip without photos), `tests/unit/smartcam-local.test.ts` (18 cases on the real-world parsing layer: plate/frame/engine OCR-text candidates with glyph confusions, current and legacy province prefixes, stable-frame voting, adaptive sampling, the cloud budget ledger, and created-id correlation that rejects misaligned or non-v4 lists), `tests/e2e/smartcam-ocr-runtime.spec.mjs` (runtime proof with the actual Tesseract worker, same-origin WASM core and language data: a real Chromium page performs genuine OCR on a cleanly rendered plate and matches it uniquely with zero `ai-assist` requests; skips honestly when the language CDN is unreachable) and `tests/e2e/smart-camera.spec.mjs` (known plate → profile with zero writes; unknown plate → intake prefill saved only after confirmation, photo attached through the storage gateway using the trusted `vehicle_ids` — the spec asserts `register_vehicle_image.p_vehicle_id` equals the id the import returned, and runs with on-device OCR disabled so no WASM is downloaded; consent refusal sends no image).

`node scripts/check-edge-types.mjs` checks the Edge sources against installed Supabase TypeScript types and a minimal Deno runtime declaration when Deno is absent. It does not verify Deno''s remote module resolution. Password resets first gate existing sessions, preserve a pending-reset state while Auth credentials change, and record the new temporary-password fingerprint before allowing self-service completion. Self-admin resets use the native change/recovery path; unrelated profile edits do not reset password-change proof.

Hosted GoTrue password updates, actual provider OCR accuracy, deployed Edge policies, real phone cameras/voice permissions and provider spending controls remain live integration checks. Test frame-number recognition against real representative documents before considering document extraction production ready.

References: [Structured outputs](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs), [image inputs](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/images-vision), [OpenAI data controls](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data).', 'MANAGER', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md'),
  ('ux-friction-audit-preamble', 'Kiểm ma sát trải nghiệm', null, '# UX Friction Audit — Xe CRM

Audited from the existing routed source on 2026-09-30. The business flow remains **Thu vào → Tồn kho → Chi phí / cập nhật → Bán ra**. Counts below describe the normal path and exclude optional fields; elapsed-time budgets are targets, not measured claims about staff productivity.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md'),
  ('ux-friction-audit-1', 'Kiểm ma sát trải nghiệm', 'Existing workflow evidence and friction', '## Existing workflow evidence and friction

| Workflow              | Existing screens and normal interactions                                                                                                                              | Required typing / repeated data                                                                                                   | Waiting, confirmation and navigation friction                                                                                                                               |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Login                 | `/login`: username, password, Đăng nhập (3 interactions, plus optional remember selection)                                                                            | Username and password; browser-appropriate autocomplete already available                                                         | Username lookup, Auth, profile and server access checks must complete. These checks remain authoritative; convenience must not skip them.                                   |
| Thu xe                | `/acquisitions/new`: open form; type frame, brand, model, purchase amount for financial roles; submit (at least 6 interactions)                                       | Common brand/model/color manually retyped; 15 inputs visible across two cards for financial roles, including optional metadata                | Long mobile scroll to the final action. Duplicate frame found only after submission. No draft recovery. Server confirmation is required.                                    |
| Find vehicle          | Top bar → `/vehicles?q=…` or search palette → detail                                                                                                                  | Plate, frame, code, engine, brand/model; prior implementation already had a palette but no real request debounce                  | `useDeferredValue` delays rendering, not requests. Every changed query could issue another request. Keyboard result selection and role-aware commands were incomplete.      |
| Open vehicle / return | `/vehicles` → `/vehicles/:id` → inventory                                                                                                                             | Query persisted in URL; status, brand/date/price filters, sort and pagination were local component state                          | Layout scrolled to the top on every pathname change. Back lost local filters/page. Recent vehicles could be displayed, but successful detail loads did not record activity. |
| Add expense           | Vehicle → scroll to expense card → `/expenses?kind=vehicle&vehicle=…&new=1` → choose type, description, amount/date → save → return to vehicle (about 8 interactions) | Vehicle context existed in the URL, but the larger screen/picker still consumed attention. Common expense description typed again | Full page transition interrupted vehicle work. Existing quick modal was not connected; several chip categories did not match existing expense enums.                        |
| Sell vehicle          | Vehicle → `/vehicles/:id/sell` → customer, phone, amount/payment → confirm (about 5–7 interactions after selection)                                                   | Vehicle and asking price already preserved; date already defaults to Vietnam today; “Đã thu đủ tiền” already existed              | Money fields displayed raw digits; no remembered safe payment category. Server confirmation must remain deliberate.                                                         |
| View inventory        | `/vehicles`: query, status, sort, filters and pagination                                                                                                              | Re-entered filters after returning from detail                                                                                    | Loading replaced the whole list on changed query keys. Dashboard status/cost/age links were not read by the inventory page.                                                 |
| Recent transactions   | Dashboard → Bán ra or Thu vào → date/search filter → transaction/vehicle                                                                                              | Date/search context could be re-entered                                                                                           | Dashboard cards were clickable in the current worktree, but links did not consistently forward the selected reporting period.                                               |
| Vehicle photos        | Detail/form → choose photos → wait for sequential upload                                                                                                              | Select files again after failure                                                                                                  | Original size gate rejected phone photos above 5 MB before compression. No local preview or per-photo retry state; uploader blocked further selections.                     |

### Existing conveniences that were not complete

The worktree already contained `MoneyInput`, `AutocompleteInput`, `QuickChips`, `QuickExpenseModal`, image compression and recent-vehicle storage. Merely having these files did not make the routed workflows faster. The main forms/detail page did not consume them. Recent storage also used device-wide keys, so shared-device users could see another account’s history. The money parser stripped arbitrary characters and could turn a malformed or negative entry into another positive amount.

These concrete defects took priority over new gestures or visual redesign.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md'),
  ('ux-friction-audit-2', 'Kiểm ma sát trải nghiệm', 'Friction budget and proposed normal path', '## Friction budget and proposed normal path

| Task                       | Budget                                             | Path after incremental convenience changes                                                              |
| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Find vehicle               | Under 3 seconds after entering a useful identifier | Focus search → type → select visible result; no mandatory Enter                                         |
| Open recently used vehicle | 1 tap                                              | “Xe vừa thao tác” → vehicle                                                                             |
| Add simple vehicle expense | Under 10 seconds                                   | Vehicle “+ Chi phí” → category chip → amount → save                                                     |
| Acquire normal vehicle     | Under 30 seconds                                   | Frame → plate if present → brand/model or suggestions → price → save; optional metadata stays available |
| Sell selected vehicle      | Under 20 seconds                                   | Customer → price/payment review → explicit server-confirmed sale                                        |
| Return to inventory        | No repeated query/filter work                      | Back restores URL filters, sort, page and saved position                                                |', 'MANAGER', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md'),
  ('ux-friction-audit-3', 'Kiểm ma sát trải nghiệm', 'Implemented convenience boundaries', '## Implemented convenience boundaries

### Search, navigation and recent activity

- Search requests use a real debounce. Search matches the existing server-supported identifiers and permitted customer/transaction results.
- Inventory URL contains query, status, brand/year/date/price filters, sort, page, pending-cost and stock-age filters. This makes browser history and the detail “Tồn kho” link restore the same context.
- Cached previous inventory rows remain visible while a changed query is being fetched; an update message makes their state clear.
- Detail data is prefetched only on hover, focus or intentional touch.
- A successful detail load records actual vehicle activity using an authenticated user-specific key. Legacy device-wide recent records are ignored. No financial fields are copied into recents.
- Mobile cards keep the normal detail link and expose a visible “Thao tác” sheet. Sale only opens the normal sale form; no gesture or quick button executes a financial mutation.

### Forms and safe defaults

- Thu xe shows essential identity/brand/model/price/date/seller inputs first. Số máy, variant/year/color/km, asking price and notes remain in an accessible “Thông tin khác” disclosure.
- Brand/model/variant/color autocomplete derives from recent values and permitted recent store vehicles. Model/variant suggestions follow the selected brand. Chips are optional shortcuts; manual input remains available.
- Money input accepts normalized VND paste and supported shorthand, displays the interpreted value, and rejects negative, malformed, fractional raw VND and unsafe amounts. Persisted money remains an integer.
- Frame duplicate warnings appear after a 450 ms debounce and link to the existing record. This is advisory convenience; server uniqueness and permission checks still decide the transaction.
- Local drafts are versioned, user-specific and expire after seven days. They restore the form''s full business content — specs, prices, seller/customer contacts and notes — so an interrupted entry resumes completely after an explicit resume or discard. Credentials, identity-document numbers, status, permissions and secrets stay excluded.
- Draft storage failure (private mode/quota) triggers close/reload loss protection and confirmation for an internal link that leaves the form; successful persistence never blocks navigation because the draft is restored next visit. The current BrowserRouter does not provide a blocker for a native Back action. Drafts are never described as completed transactions.
- Primary acquisition/edit/sale actions stay reachable on mobile. Dates use `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh` and stay visible/editable.
- A successful acquisition opens the real vehicle with next actions: Thu xe tiếp, Thêm ảnh and permitted Chi phí. Success comes from the confirmed RPC, not an arbitrary query string.
- AI review handoffs, when explicitly selected by the user, prefill only safe structured acquisition fields. Purchase prices must be entered by the user. An expense handoff displays a review notice and requires the normal explicit save.

### Vehicle context and photos

- Detail “+ Chi phí” and the mobile vehicle sheet open the same compact form with a fixed vehicle ID. Existing `canManage` expense permissions remain unchanged; STAFF does not receive extra permissions for convenience.
- Expense chips map to the existing enum: Lốp/Nhớt → PARTS, Giấy tờ → PAPERWORK.
- Choosing a category supplies its description and focuses the amount. Date defaults to today. Repeating the previous expense restores only category/description and clears the amount.
- Modal focus stays inside the dialog, Escape closes a nonpending action, and focus returns to the opener. Pending financial submissions cannot be dismissed/repeated.
- Clipboard buttons copy frame, engine, plate, internal code and allowed supplier phone with explicit feedback.
- Vehicle photos show local previews immediately, compress before upload, queue in the background and expose a status/retry for each image. Another photo can be selected while uploads run. A before-unload warning protects pending uploads. Document images used by extraction are not automatically converted into vehicle photos.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md'),
  ('ux-friction-audit-4', 'Kiểm ma sát trải nghiệm', 'Validation', '## Validation

Source review covers all frequent workflows listed above. Automated validation is recorded in `docs/VERIFICATION.md`.

Meaningful convenience tests include:

- Scoped recent records and categorical values do not cross accounts; malformed/unavailable storage is handled.
- Permissions/status/secrets and identity numbers are excluded from reusable drafts; recent values never store amounts.
- Repeat expense does not store/reuse an amount.
- Strict money normalization rejects malformed/negative/unsafe values.
- Isolated mocked browser interactions cover mobile acquisition with a visible action, integer shorthand conversion, duplicate detection before submit, contextual expenses with valid enum values, repeat amount clearing, Escape/focus behavior and inventory return context.
- Browser timing checks use the budgets above against fixture interactions; they are regression checks rather than claims about a person’s typing speed. A fifth desktop regression checks Ctrl+K, recent vehicles, one debounced request while typing, and ArrowDown/Enter selection.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md'),
  ('ux-friction-audit-5', 'Kiểm ma sát trải nghiệm', 'Remaining verification and next increments', '## Remaining verification and next increments

- Perform acceptance with actual store staff on a phone and desktop: search-as-you-type, acquisition, expense, sticky save, recent vehicle, quick sheet and back/forward. Record task durations without field contents.
- Verify compression readability using representative plate/frame photos. Device-specific camera/document quality needs real hardware.
- Expand suggestions beyond the recent 100 permitted store records only if real usage shows missing frequent values.
- Current duplicate convenience query reads up to 100 matching permitted results. Server validation remains the definitive check.
- Pending image uploads continue within the current browser session; there is no persistent offline upload queue across closing/restarting the app.
- Swipe/long press and image reordering are optional future shortcuts; visible actions already cover their useful tasks. They must never execute business lifecycle/financial changes directly.
- Lightweight anonymous timing/abandonment measurement can be added after a retention/consent decision. No sensitive field contents or employee surveillance telemetry is collected by this increment.', 'MANAGER', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md'),
